WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.120
The Fast family's tenth chapter is over – or is&nbsp;
it? After that stunner of an ending, it's clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.440
that there's more story to tell in the world of&nbsp;
the Fast and the Furious. Here's what the movie's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.458
credits scene tells us about all the action&nbsp;
to come. Warning: spoilers ahead for "Fast X."

00:00:15.458 --> 00:00:19.391
In case you ran out of the theater to take&nbsp;
off on some of your own street-racing action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.391 --> 00:00:22.200
you should know there's a mid-credits&nbsp;
scene after the last shot of "Fast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.905
X" – and it has massive implications&nbsp;
for the future of the franchise.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.480
Dwayne Johnson being in the movie has&nbsp;
been spoiled for a little while now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:34.260
but the devil's in the details. When Dominic&nbsp;
Toretto and his team close the movie with a last,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.868
explosive cliffhanger, this scene&nbsp;
sets the stage for what's next.

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:42.420
The mid-credits scene shows a giant, masked&nbsp;
man decked out in high-tech military gear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.980
investigating an abandoned building.&nbsp;
Inside, the voice of Dante Reyes can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.720
be heard taunting him. Dante makes threats to&nbsp;
the masked figure, promising nothing short of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.620
a meeting with the devil to pay for his&nbsp;
sins against his father, Hernan Reyes.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.640
Then we get the big reveal. While Dom may&nbsp;
have been the one who pulled off the heist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.620
that killed Dante's father, he wasn't actually the&nbsp;
one to pull the trigger. That would be none other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:08.460
than Dwayne Johnson's larger-than-life&nbsp;
character, special agent Luke Hobbs.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:10.173
"Who the hell are you?"

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:14.940
"I'm what you call an ice cold can of whoop ass."

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.960
Right on cue, the masked man pulls down&nbsp;
his disguise and reveals the glorious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.220
goatee'd face of Luke Hobbs, returning&nbsp;
to the "Fast and Furious" universe for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:26.000
the first time since 2019's "Hobbs and Shaw."

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.100
While his presence in the movie is&nbsp;
a pretty big throwback on its own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:34.320
Hobbs' vibe in "Fast X" also feels much more&nbsp;
reminiscent of his characterization in "Fast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.640
Five." Even in this brief teaser, Johnson&nbsp;
is clearly leaning into the cartoonish,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.260
gritty rage that Hobbs exuded in his first&nbsp;
appearance in the franchise. It's a bit of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.149
a reversal from the Dwayne Johnson charm the&nbsp;
actor brought to the role in later movies like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:52.320
"The Fate of the Furious" and "Hobbs and Shaw."&nbsp;
He even grunts out a perfect "sumbitch" to boot.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.060
"Well hello, you sumbitch."

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.460
The scene is everything "Fast"&nbsp;
fans could have hoped for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:00.060
and it's especially shocking given&nbsp;
all the behind-the-scenes bluster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.420
surrounding Vin Diesel and Dwayne&nbsp;
Johnson's professional relationship.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:08.160
Johnson's return was revealed online almost&nbsp;
a week before the film's release. It likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:12.240
gave some fans flashbacks to a similar&nbsp;
incident last year, when the post-credits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:17.194
scene for Johnson's "Black Adam" was also spoiled,&nbsp;
seemingly on purpose, a week before its release.

00:02:17.301 --> 00:02:21.441
The news that Johnson was returning to the&nbsp;
Fast franchise came as a major surprise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:24.000
following a public feud and apparent fallout with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.660
Vin Diesel. The actor had previously&nbsp;
stated clearly, on multiple occasions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.460
that he had no interest in returning to The&nbsp;
Fast Saga outside of future "Hobbs and Shaw"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:37.200
sequels – even after a public appeal from&nbsp;
Diesel for his co-star to return for Fast X.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:41.520
It's possible that Johnson's initial decision&nbsp;
was made when he was planning to devote the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.900
next several years of his career to building a&nbsp;
universe around the DC Comics character Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:50.520
Adam – plans that seem to have been scuttled&nbsp;
after a change in leadership at DC Studios.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.200
Perhaps the decision not to rejoin was more&nbsp;
professional than personal, and the cancellation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.805
of future "Black Adam" sequels gave Johnson&nbsp;
space to re-commit to the "Fast" franchise.

00:02:59.805 --> 00:03:03.420
In any case, Hobbs' return to the "Fast&nbsp;
and Furious" universe can really only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.080
be a great thing, as the character&nbsp;
opens up more organic storytelling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:11.040
opportunities for the upcoming sequels to&nbsp;
explore. Perhaps they could even finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.120
reveal the true identity of the Eteon&nbsp;
director introduced in "Hobbs and Shaw."

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.260
Regardless of how it shakes out in future&nbsp;
films, it's just exciting to see Johnson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:23.400
returning to one of his most iconic roles.&nbsp;
We're going to have a hard time waiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:27.715
for his reunion with the rest of Toretto's&nbsp;
crew in the upcoming sequels to "Fast X."

